        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART X, LINE 2:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE CLUB IS EXEMPT FROM INCOME TAXES UNDER SECTION 501(C)(7) OF THE INTERNAL REVENUE CODE, EXCEPT FOR AMOUNTS REPRESENTING UNRELATED BUSINESS INCOME. THE CLUB IS SIMILARLY EXEMPT FOR STATE PURPOSES. UNRELATED BUSINESS INCOME CONSISTS OF NET INCOME FROM NON-MEMBER ACTIVITIES AND INTEREST INCOME. THE CLUB FOLLOWS ACCOUNTING STANDARDS WHICH CLARIFY THE ACCOUNTING FOR UNCERTAINTY IN INCOME TAXES RECOGNIZED IN THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS AND PRESCRIBES A RECOGNITION THRESHOLD AND MEASUREMENT ATTRIBUTE FOR THE FINANCIAL STATEMENT RECOGNITION AND MEASUREMENT OF A TAX POSITION TAKEN OR EXPECTED TO BE TAKEN IN A TAX RETURN. IT ALSO PROVIDES GUIDANCE ON DERECOGNITION AND MEASUREMENT OF A TAX POSITION TAKEN OR TO BE TAKEN IN A TAX RETURN. AS OF DECEMBER 31, 2024, THE CLUB HAS NOT ACCRUED INTEREST OR PENALTIES TO UNCERTAIN TAX POSITIONS.</ExplanationTxt>
